From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:16:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] The honesty copy deck: every flag and the sentence it
 owes the founder

Eleven facts travel on every range because a number would otherwise mislead, and
none of them reached a founder. This is the deck that closes it, with the firing
counts across the 21 real profiles so the common path is visible: a RANGE, drawn
from ADJACENT names, partial or strong overlap, bounded, on a mixed basis. The
bounded sentence and the closeness sentence will be read more than the rest put
together.

Three rules run through it. Say the fact then say what to do with it, because a
caveat that only warns makes the product look weaker while one that tells the
founder how to use the number makes it look expert. Never apologise for the data:
'only two comparables' is an apology, 'two companies have priced this business
model recently and here they are' is a finding. And print the working where we
have it, since shared_words, control_names, sole and the regression scatter are
all printable.

One warning included rather than left implicit: eleven caveats on a screen is
noise, not honesty. At most two inline, ranked by severity, rest behind a
disclosure.
